        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 24 at 1:07PM MST until September 24 at 1:45PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ</headline>
        <description>SVRTWC

The National Weather Service in Tucson has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
East Central Pima County in southeastern Arizona...

* Until 145 PM MST.

* At 107 PM MST, a severe thunderstorm was located near Corona De
Tucson, moving north at 5 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to
roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Tucson, Vail, Corona De Tucson, East Sahuarita, Summit, Tucson
International Airport and Rita Ranch.

This includes the following highways...
Interstate 10 between mile markers 267 and 282. Route 83 near mile
marker 58.
</description>
        <instruction>Seek shelter inside a well-built structure and stay away from
windows. This storm is capable of producing damaging winds and large
hail.</instruction>
